From f0e63454a0099c46dede0f2ea9ad021064e04636 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:34:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vise): self-centering grip jaw - a step the stock sits
 on

The self-centering vise gains an optional grip step beside the dovetail
lip: grip_depth (ledge below the jaw top) and grip_width (ledge reach
from the clamping face), 0 = off. The jaw mesh carries the step and the
frame's z = 0 is the ledge, so the stock seats on it and the fixture
laws judge the stepped jaw. Refused by name: one figure without the
other, both with a dovetail, depth >= jaw height, width >= jaw
thickness, ledges meeting at the opening. Project key additive (written
only when on), dialog rows with tooltips, MCP dimensions.

Fixes #1274

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
